; Hints.inix -- what each control in a FileDir dialog does, in one sentence, spoken by Shift+F1.
; A section is a dialog's title as its window shows it; a key is a control's name, without its
; underline letter or trailing colon. [All dialogs] holds names that mean the same everywhere.
; A control with no hint here says the first sentence of its own description instead.
; Your own copy, in %LOCALAPPDATA%\FileDir\configs, wins over this one, so you can change a hint.

[All dialogs]
OK = Carries out the command with what you have entered and closes the dialog; Control+Enter does this from any control.
Cancel = Closes the dialog and changes nothing; Escape does this from any control.
Help = Opens this dialog's help, which F1 also does from any control.
Close = Closes this window.
Folder = The folder to use; type its path, or pick one with the buttons below. If it does not exist, FileDir offers to create it.
Browse = Opens the Windows folder picker, to find the folder by looking through the drives.
Current = Lists the folders open in FileDir now; Enter picks one.
Recent = Lists the folders you have visited recently; Enter picks one.
Quick = Lists your Quick folders, the ones you keep shortcuts to; Enter picks one.
Special = Lists the special folders of Windows, such as Documents, Downloads and AppData Local; Enter picks one.

[Copy To]
Folder = The folder the marked items are copied into.

[Move To]
Folder = The folder the marked items are moved into; they leave the folder they are in now.

[Open Folder]
Folder = The folder to open in a new FileDir window.

[Target Folder]
Folder = The folder the command puts its results in.

[Unarchive To]
Folder = The folder the archive's files are put into; files with the same names there are replaced.

[Unarchive Password]
UnarchivePassword = The password of the archive, used for every archive you unpack until FileDir closes.

[Rename]
Name = The item's new name, with its extension.

[New Folder]
Folder = The name of the new folder, made in the folder you are in.

[Input]
Name = The name to give the new item.
Value = The value to use.

[Jump]
Text = The start of an item's name; FileDir moves to the first item that begins with it.

[Keywords]
Text = Words to find in the items' names; FileDir moves to the next item holding them.

[Keywords back]
Text = Words to find in the items' names; FileDir moves back to the previous item holding them.

[Filter]
Expression = Which items to show, such as *.txt or *2026*; the others are hidden until the filter is cleared.

[Mark with Regex]
Text = A regular expression; every item whose name matches it is marked.

[Extract with Regex]
Text = A regular expression; the text it matches in the current file is copied out.

[Evaluate]
Expression = A calculation, such as 3 * (4 + 5); FileDir says the answer.

[Web Address]
Address = The web address to download or open, starting with http or https.

[FTP Address]
Address = The FTP address to connect to, starting with ftp.

[Download Extensions]
Extensions = The kinds of file to download from a page, by extension, separated by spaces, such as pdf docx.

[Path List Extensions]
Extensions = The kinds of file to list, by extension, separated by spaces, such as txt md.

[Translate File]
Language to translate into = The language to translate the current file into, such as Spanish or French.

[Chat with AI]
Question = Your question for the AI; its answer is spoken and shown.

[Chat about File]
Question = Your question about the current file; the AI answers from the file's contents.

; [Main window] (10 November 2026): the folder window, whose title changes with the folder; keyed by the control's role.
[Main window]
role List=The files and folders in this folder, one per line.
role Table=The files and folders in this folder, one per line.
